  "goodToKnow": "Horten means to hoard: Lebensmittel, Geld, Gold horten. In spring 2020, panic buying (Hamsterkäufe, from the hamster that stuffs its cheeks) left supermarket shelves empty of toilet paper. Der Hort means a hoard or treasure, as in the Nibelungenhort, and also an after-school club for primary pupils (der Kinderhort). Regular: hortete, gehortet."
